                <pb facs="0518" n="446" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 22372/1.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Caldera to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-11-17"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                    1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Caldera says it is reported that the two Americans captured with the
                    revolutionists have been executed, and says he has reason to believe the report
                    is true.</p>
            </div>
